    "background_story": "Shmoopie was a small, family-owned winery that had been producing high-quality wines for generations. However, they were struggling to stand out in a crowded market. That was until they made the bold decision to switch to screwtop closures for all of their bottles. The move was met with skepticism by some, but Shmoopie's owners were convinced that it was the way forward. And they were right. The screwtops not only made their wines more convenient for consumers, but also helped to reduce waste and preserve the quality of the wine. As a result, Shmoopie's sales began to soar, and they became known as one of the most innovative and eco-friendly wineries in the region. Their flagship wine, a crisp and refreshing Sauvignon Blanc, became a particular favorite among wine enthusiasts, and Shmoopie's reputation as a producer of high-quality, screwtop wines was cemented.",
